.60.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=14,$ giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=28,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{3.60}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=14$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & ≈\\frac{14-28}{\\sqrt{3.60}} \\\\  & ≈-7.38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94460/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc94085c-4088-5eaf-887a-eea7f040573c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94460"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332017/field-1/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80" :answer/id #uuid "bfd721f8-e1b0-57dc-9ebd-08d58e4a0866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332017/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2c4d289-d11d-518e-95bc-be0a3a0f7059" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332017/field-1/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80" :answer-field/choices ["q-332017/field-1/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332017" :question/id #uuid "c66cb5df-fa02-5bb5-968c-7fa0e49b7e4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-332017" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{―}{x}=4$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.25.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=3.4.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=4,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{0.25}=0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=3.4$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{3.4-4}{0.5} \\\\  & =-1.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332017/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc94085c-4088-5eaf-887a-eea7f040573c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332017"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457/selection/6f5e077d315529d6d052dede51f9a20ad13f74b5ed335ea855fcd677982b06c0" :answer/id #uuid "c325b34e-5a42-5d44-9fcb-f6eff3d2c0b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.46" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457/selection/314ef179ed0e3368fe51721c1ec8c6ee48dd87229b31064ac4c9db53bb58ce67" :answer/id #uuid "2d11fefc-4b0b-5192-9a22-6d1922f7c366" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457/selection/0acc180430d77f9f3cbcefdfcfc3ca002eb723cd798394ff93fa72f0c963e70c" :answer/id #uuid "3f6442b8-3dac-5784-8697-c28a4fd9998b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457/selection/c02946f63768b10740f17e5860a69998aaf22d3527d0628645d88ef191e762af" :answer/id #uuid "1c3dd489-4f7b-548f-bcc7-80627d5105be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457/selection/191439dce3c9d52814395c0c5f12330e822bc4574b0dac496feb2b8b0ef1e0f2" :answer/id #uuid "0373ecd7-a713-5501-9dcc-9fb43d79a741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb82b16b-6758-5142-a87b-345d298408d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94457/selection/0acc180430d77f9f3cbcefdfcfc3ca002eb723cd798394ff93fa72f0c963e70c" :answer-field/choices ["q-94457/selection/6f5e077d315529d6d052dede51f9a20ad13f74b5ed335ea855fcd677982b06c0" "q-94457/selection/314ef179ed0e3368fe51721c1ec8c6ee48dd87229b31064ac4c9db53bb58ce67" "q-94457/selection/0acc180430d77f9f3cbcefdfcfc3ca002eb723cd798394ff93fa72f0c963e70c" "q-94457/selection/c02946f63768b10740f17e5860a69998aaf22d3527d0628645d88ef191e762af" "q-94457/selection/191439dce3c9d52814395c0c5f12330e822bc4574b0dac496feb2b8b0ef1e0f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94457" :question/id #uuid "e3ffce57-1bac-5c81-b423-d3a26144e3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-94457" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=10.8.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=10.5,$ giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=6,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{10.8}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=10.5$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & ≈\\frac{10.5-6}{\\sqrt{10.8}} \\\\  & ≈1.37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94457/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc94085c-4088-5eaf-887a-eea7f040573c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332024/field-1/96a17d2f9c8e47adb4f0bab66abc903cee02da1f75cabba07db22a912d67391e" :answer/id #uuid "ff465509-e151-58d7-af35-68de76fffbc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.59" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332024/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6291258d-3f41-5b6c-8881-0e47a2c2bd58" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332024/field-1/96a17d2f9c8e47adb4f0bab66abc903cee02da1f75cabba07db22a912d67391e" :answer-field/choices ["q-332024/field-1/96a17d2f9c8e47adb4f0bab66abc903cee02da1f75cabba07db22a912d67391e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332024" :question/id #uuid "387cd435-3846-537c-8dbc-b4fbba04f51d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332024" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{―}{x}=-1.2$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.32.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=-2.1,$ rounding your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=-1.2,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{0.32}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=-2.1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.1-(-1.2)}{\\sqrt{0.32}} \\\\  & ≈-1.59,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332024/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc94085c-4088-5eaf-887a-eea7f040573c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332211/field-1/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "20507df9-b2ce-5562-85d0-d7af8c6882a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332211/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5affb72-7c6d-54fa-b613-74d83e2e19d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332211/field-1/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer-field/choices ["q-332211/field-1/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332211" :question/id #uuid "1e36ba23-9627-5e17-aefa-a4e6e5a83ed6" :question/math-academy-id "q-332211" :question/problem "A data set has a mean $\\overset{―}{x}=-0.3$ and a standard deviation $\\sigma =0.5.$ An observation of the data set has a $z$-score $z=1.4.$ Find the value $x$ of this observation.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{―}{x}=-0.3,$ $z=1.4,$ and $\\sigma =0.5$ into the formula and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ x & =-0.3+1.4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\ x & =-0.3+0.7 \\\\ x & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332211/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2169053d-78fc-5714-82f4-d89fc36ff695"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17237/selection/e8a7f2617d34ac3f4b7ee4434b0400806f613368b7a087e343c93b76500c56db" :answer/id #uuid "c7375dc1-6e51-5fbc-ae21-71a1ddfc5746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42.95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17237/selection/3fc6fbca1f3a72d8942d2bea24d991e7f52af5bf283e1e858a74cb193babb359" :answer/id #uuid "e6024899-5431-5cba-aebc-9259f96ef5d9" :answer/type :answer.type/mat