,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=35.4,$ $z=-1.1,$ and $\\sigma =10.5$ into the formula and solving for $\\overset{―}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 35.4 & =\\overset{―}{x}+(-1.1)\\cdot 10.5 \\\\ 35.4 & =\\overset{―}{x}-11.55 \\\\ \\overset{―}{x} & =46.95.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17237/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2169053d-78fc-5714-82f4-d89fc36ff695"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17237"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332047/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6b7835d7-6985-579c-a75b-2629635c5ada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332047/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b3d0569-b81e-5762-84aa-c02470a2f6a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332047/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-332047/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332047" :question/id #uuid "26bebcb6-0fc4-55f8-8377-c7bba785f83f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332047" :question/problem "A data set has a mean $\\overset{―}{x}=10$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=12.1$ and $z$-score $z=1.05.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=12.1,$ $\\overset{―}{x}=10,$ and $z=1.05$ int