04fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332239" :question/id #uuid "e64b9681-ce05-59b7-b509-eed464a28ad6" :question/math-academy-id "q-332239" :question/problem "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=3.08,{x}_{2}=8.68$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=-1.2$ and ${z}_{2}=2.3,$ respectively. Find the mean $\\overset{¯}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{¯}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n3.08=\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n8.68=\\overset{¯}{x}+2.3\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8.68-3.08 & =(2.3-(-1.2))\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.6 & =3.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this value back into our first equation and solving for $\\overset{¯}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot 1.6 \\\\ 3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}-1.92 \\\\ \\overset{¯}{x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332239/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01100ea8-2ab9-511e-8321-6ef5588c4417"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332238/field-1/aa21066db5c66f5e02b959020a028876be8453fb3a587a557a61c6dc14fec257" :answer/id #uuid "d1090a83-422d-5de2-a634-12d4721babc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332238/field-1/0338269526941c96d6177f55be1449945483a80ce5b6cf2ec758893c9b730620" :answer/id #uuid "10833697-a385-5ae