swer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332248/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer-field/choices ["q-332248/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-332248/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332248" :question/id #uuid "2740c50b-5c9f-5ee1-8ec5-a13a1b5ce0ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-332248" :question/problem "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=0.5,{x}_{2}=4.5$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=-3$ and ${z}_{2}=5,$ respectively. Find the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the data set.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n0.5=\\overset{¯}{x}+(-3)\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n4.5=\\overset{¯}{x}+5\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4.5-0.5 & =(5-(-3))\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 4 & =8\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332248/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01100ea8-2ab9-511e-8321-6ef5588c4417"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332248"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332233/field-1/acb11913e40f66990ef37d5f8d45159f9639ad6d7e0b6d5fbf3b8692ed1dfedc" :answer/id #uuid "6088d170-501b-583e-8cf3-e3f735ef1911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332233/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a5d33e6-4075-50a0-8f93-0b3ab4d62ff1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332233/field-1/acb11913e40f66990ef37d5f8d45159f9639ad6d7e0b6d5fbf3b8692ed1dfedc" :answer-field/choices ["q-332233/field-1/acb11913e40f66990ef37d5f8d45159f9639ad6d7e0b6d5fbf3b8692ed1dfedc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332233" :question/id #uuid "aae1f933-06ba-565d-aaa7-cd1446205445" :question/math-academy-id "q-332233" :question/problem "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=-1.2,{x}_{2}=2.8$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=-0.5$ and ${z}_{2}=2,$ respectively. Find the mean $\\overset{¯}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{¯}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n-1.2=\\overset{¯}{x}+(-0.5)\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n2.8=\\overset{¯}{x}+2\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.8-(-1.2) & =(2-(-0.5))\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 4 & =2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this value back into our first equation and solving for $\\overset{¯}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1.2 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-0.5)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -1.2 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-0.5)\\cdot 1.6 \\\\ -1.2 & =\\overset{¯}{x}-0.8 \\\\ \\overset{¯}{x} & =-0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332233/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01100ea8-2ab9-511e-8321-6ef5588c4417"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332257/field-1/1ef14df341e2f354c34ae93e3c7ddfea65840e9fda1897b5ea50de018c5615fe" :answer/id #uuid "f2bf24a8-fb46-511e-ba8e-19fe8162dfc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332257/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ec31e32-7a9a-513f-83ff-89322270293d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332257/field-1/1ef14df341e2f354c34ae93e3c7ddfea65840e9fda1897b5ea50de018c5615fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-332257/field-1/1ef14df341e2f354c34ae93e3c7ddfea65840e9fda1897b5ea50de018c5615fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332257" :question/id #uuid "1dd8a745-3186-5132-97bd-1381104984bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-332257" :question/problem "The mean heart rate of a group of patients during light exercise is $\\overset{¯}{x}=70$ beats per minute. A particular patient in this group has a heart rate of $74$ beats per minute, and his $z$-score is $z=2.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the patients' heart rates in the group.\n\nThe standard deviation of the heart rates is\n{{field-1}}\nbeats per minute." :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{―}{x}=70,$ $z=2.5,$ and $x=74$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 74 & =70+2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 4 & =2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{4}{2.5} \\\\ \\sigma  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard deviation of the patients' heart rates in the group is $1.6$ beats per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332257/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519/selection/b93b62940f6b6ee8e93156353050a3fcaf49eded6ae7c264596e2f475a34b564" :answer/id #uuid "e21359d4-427e-5120-9b37-fffe6a7a05d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.2\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519/selection/4f6d38a7b1129150861b5400ca58ddbe2ee89e8884392581d36bd2b5c295c4cb" :answer/id #uuid "0b54f4bb-1c40-51ec-8cbf-16b9a107e56d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.0\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519/selection/c760cfeddf94bdd854ab18a514fcc4302cc66fd8dba05bf834995cc549f3ebab" :answer/id #uuid "27378599-e318-5d19-90b8-470801cf9ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519/selection/4340dd8b6f3d516ad3b48e7fd12241c2c12e057377bceef8f7611a403ffef713" :answer/id #uuid "3eaa3cc4-4ad7-576a-a85b-e1836857c25e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.0\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519/selection/1a2bbd04c38e4a337f40b5f148dca493f0a374e7f338b5290338db6f2b9ee9b1" :answer/id #uuid "baa3524a-ecd7-5498-b8a1-664d224cb597" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "08d47a6b-ce31-52d9-a089-f62202f25e3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94519/selection/c760cfeddf94bdd854ab18a514fcc4302cc66fd8dba05bf834995cc549f3ebab" :answer-field/choices ["q-94519/selection/b93b62940f6b6ee8e93156353050a3fcaf49eded6ae7c264596e2f475a34b564" "q-94519/selection/4f6d38a7b1129150861b5400ca58ddbe2ee89e8884392581d36bd2b5c295c4cb" "q-94519/selection/c760cfeddf94bdd854ab18a514fcc4302cc66fd8dba05bf834995cc549f3ebab" "q-94519/selection/4340dd8b6f3d516ad3b48e7fd12241c2c12e057377bceef8f7611a403ffef713" "q-94519/selection/1a2bbd04c38e4a337f40b5f148dca493f0a374e7f338b5290338db6f2b9ee9b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94519" :question/id #uuid "9d4c2dcb-2073-5bfd-816d-d45085c526dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-94519" :question/problem "The mean weight of a group of ballet dancers is $45\\text{ kg}.$ One of the dancers in the ballet group weighs $38\\text{ kg}$, and her $z$-score is $-2.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the weight of the dancers in the ballet group." :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=38,$ $\\overset{―}{x}=45,$ and $z=-2.5$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 38 & =45+(-2.5)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -7 & =-2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{-7}{-2.5} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the standard deviation of the ballet dancer's weights is $2.8\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94519/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94519"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170517/selection/f27801bb4c5089dbf65a18f807e73b17fa5df0df4933e897d13dcdc495cb21f8" :answer/id #uuid "952cfd09-0848-595e-bfd1-6a45cdf0479d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170517/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "7fbb8e9f-0c7e-562a-b3fb-e0583283b639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170517/selection/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d" :answer/id #uuid "944cb518-4232-559b-96d5-fe92d13c54ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170517/selection/d