estion/problem "The mean score on a national mathematics contest is $\\overset{¯}{x}=80$ points with a standard deviation of $5$ points. What is the $z\\text{-score}$ that corresponds to a student's score of $65$ points?\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=65$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{¯}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{65-80}{5} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332254/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
